SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Futures of Listening x Immersive Audio Network:
  Residency Open Call (Bristol\, IAN Festival 2027)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 21 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nOne residency for a freelan
 ce audio practitioner (composer\, sound designer\, audio maker\, artist or
  researcher) registered in the Netherlands\, to develop an existing projec
 t into a spatial\, story-led sound work.\n\nOrganisation: Futures of Liste
 ning (FIBER\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek\, Art of Sound) and the Immersive Audio
  Network (IAN)\nLocation: Bristol\, UK (Arnolfini and IAN's mobile Immersi
 ve Audio Lab). Open only to practitioners registered with the Dutch Chambe
 r of Commerce (KvK).\nAward: EUR 1\,750 residency fee (excl. VAT\, paid on
  invoice)\, plus return travel from the Netherlands to Bristol and private
  accommodation for 22 to 30 January 2027. No application fee.\nDuration: 5
 -day residency\, 22 to 27 January 2027\, with a public work-in-progress pr
 esentation at the IAN Festival on 29 January 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.fi
 ber-space.nl/news/open-call-futures-of-listening-x-immersive-audio-network
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fiber-space.nl/news/open-call-futures-of-listening-x-immers
 ive-audio-network/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Bristol\, UK (Arnolfini and IAN's mobile Immersive Audio Lab). Ope
 n only to practitioners registered with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK
 ).
END:VEVENT
